1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:03,797
A child swallowed a button battery, or you think they might have?

2
00:00:03,797 --> 00:00:04,943
This is an emergency.

3
00:00:05,750 --> 00:00:10,977
Stuck in the food pipe, it creates a current that can burn through tissue in as little as 2 hours.

4
00:00:12,250 --> 00:00:16,775
1 — Go to the emergency room right away, or call emergency services.

5
00:00:16,775 --> 00:00:18,373
Don't wait for symptoms.

6
00:00:19,070 --> 00:00:24,638
2 — Don't make them vomit, and don't give food or drink unless a medical professional tells you to.

7
00:00:25,340 --> 00:00:29,308
3 — If you can, bring the battery packaging or a matching battery.

8
00:00:30,340 --> 00:00:34,227
Signs can be subtle: drooling, coughing, pain swallowing, vomiting.

9
00:00:34,227 --> 00:00:35,097
Or none at all.

10
00:00:36,340 --> 00:00:40,905
Prevent it: keep batteries and gadgets out of reach, and tape battery covers shut.
